ER</span>/<span class=3D"kwb">VEHICLE</span> models. Such models have the <=
span class=3D"kwb">FRAME</span> keyword, as do some other large models. Whe=
never a rule refers to a model=E2=80=99s position in relation to anything e=
lse on the battlefield (e.g. when <a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed=
/the-rules/core-rules/#Measuring-Distances">measuring distances</a>), if th=
at model has the <span class=3D"kwb">FRAME</span> keyword, unless otherwise=
 stated, measure to and from the closest point on that model (so not necess=
arily from its base, if it has one).<br><br>When rotating a <span class=3D"=
kwb">FRAME</span> model as part of a move, if that model does not have a ba=
se, turn it any amount around its central axis, while keeping it upright.
