Some rules enable a player, weapon, model or unit to ignore <a href=3D"http=
s://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/rules-appendix/#Modifiers">modifiers</=
a>. When using such rules, the following points apply:<br><br>Unless otherw=
ise stated, that rule allows you to ignore modifiers to the unit=E2=80=99s =
rolls and the unit=E2=80=99s profile and weapon characteristics.<br><br>Whe=
n a rule states you can ignore modifiers to a stated roll or characteristic=
, you can choose to ignore all of those modifiers, or only some of them. Fo=
r example, you can still choose to apply positive/beneficial modifiers whil=
e ignoring negative/detrimental modifiers.<br><br><div class=3D"redExample"=
><b style=3D"font-style:normal">Example:</b> Your unit can ignore character=
istic modifiers and is under the effect of +2" <b>M</b> and -2" <b>M</b>. Y=
ou can choose to ignore the -2" <b>M</b>, meaning that unit=E2=80=99s <b>M<=
/b> characteristic will only be modified by the +2" <b>M</b>.</div><br><div=
 class=3D"redExample"><b style=3D"font-style:normal">Example:</b> Your unit=
=E2=80=99s ranged attacks can ignore roll modifiers and are under the effec=
t of +1 to <b><b><a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-r=
ules/#1.-Hit-Roll">hit rolls</a></b></b> and -1 to <b>hit rolls</b>. You ca=
n choose to ignore the -1 to <b>hit rolls</b>, meaning those attacks will o=
nly be affected by the +1 to <b>hit rolls</b>.</div>
</span></div><div class=3D"tooltip_templates"><span id=3D"tooltip_content00=
