awneagle Jetbike</a></div></div><div style=3D"clear:both"></div></div></spa=
n></span></span></div><div class=3D"tooltip_templates"><span id=3D"tooltip_=
content00053"><div class=3D"tooltip_header">13.08 Benefit of Cover</div><a =
href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Benefit-of-Cov=
er"><div class=3D"tooltip_link"></div></a><div style=3D"clear:both"></div>
Each time a ranged attack targets a unit, if <u>every</u> model in that uni=
t meets one or more of the following conditions, that unit has the <b>benef=
it of cover</b> against that attack:<br><ul><li>That model has the <span cl=
ass=3D"kwb">INFANTRY</span>/<span class=3D"kwb">BEASTS</span>/<span class=
=3D"kwb">SWARM</span> keyword and is within a <b><b><a href=3D"https://waha=
pedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Placing-Terrain">terrain area</a><=
/b></b>.</li><li>That model is not <b><b><a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh=
40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Visibility">fully visible</a></b></b> to the =
attacking model due to one or more intervening <b>terrain features</b> and/=
or one or more intervening <b><a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the=
-rules/core-rules/#Obscuring">obscuring terrain areas</a></b> (see below).<=
/li></ul><br>Each time a ranged attack targets a unit that has the <b>benef=
it of cover</b> against it, worsen the <b>BS</b> characteristic of that att=
ack by 1.
<div class=3D"faqErrataStrat"><div class=3D"faqErrataSpoiler"><div class=3D=
"faqErrataHead"><h3>FAQ</h3></div><div class=3D"faqErrataSpoilerBody"><div =
class=3D"faq BreakInsideAvoid"><table width=3D"100%" border=3D"0" bordercol=
or=3D"#888" cellspacing=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"4"><tbody><tr class=3D"faq_Q_l=
ine"><td align=3D"center" class=3D"faq_Q">Q:</td><td><i>When my unit shoots=
 at another unit, how does it work if <b>some</b> models in the target unit=
 are <b><span class=3D"tooltip00015" data-tooltip-content=3D"#tooltip_conte=
nt00015"><span class=3D"tt kwbu">fully</span> <span class=3D"tt kwbu">visib=
le</span></span></b> to <b>some</b> models in my unit, while others are wit=
hin a <b><b><span class=3D"tooltip00001" data-tooltip-content=3D"#tooltip_c=
ontent00001"><span class=3D"tt kwbu">terrain</span> <span class=3D"tt kwbu"=
>area</span></span></b></b>/not <b>fully visible</b>?</i></td></tr><tr><td =
align=3D"center" class=3D"faq_A">A:</td><td><div style=3D"margin-top:1px">F=
or each attacking model in your unit, determine whether the target unit has=
 the <b>benefit of cover</b>, as described in <a href=3D"https://wahapedia.=
ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Terrain-and-Visibility">Terrain and Visi=
bility</a>. In this scenario, the target unit will likely have the <b>benef=
it of cover</b> against <u>some</u> of the attacking models, but not all.<b=
r><br>This means that, in an example unit where all attacking models are us=
ing the same weapon, when you get to the <a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh=
40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#3.-Resolve-Attacks">Resolve Attacks step</a> =
of the Attack Sequence, you will collect dice for attacks made by models ag=
ainst which the target unit has the <b>benefit of cover</b> separately from=
 the dice for attacks made by models against which the target unit does not=
 have the <b>benefit of cover</b>.</div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div></div></div>
