Terrain">terrain feature</a></b></b> has the <b>Solid</b> rule (<span class=
=3D"kwn"><a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#So=
lid">13.11</a></span>), as <b><b><a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/=
the-rules/core-rules/#Dense">dense terrain features</a></b></b> do, a model=
 cannot end a move such that any part of it is through any enclosed part of=
 that <b>terrain feature</b> that is 3" or less from ground level =E2=80=93=
 not even through small openings such as doors and windows. This ensures th=
at protruding elements of models cannot be used to circumvent the <b><a hre=
f=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Visibility">visib=
ility</a></b> restrictions of the <b>Solid</b> rule.
</span></div><div class=3D"tooltip_templates"><span id=3D"tooltip_content00=
061"><div class=3D"tooltip_header">13.06 Terrain and Movement</div><a href=
=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Terrain-and-Moveme=
nt"><div class=3D"tooltip_link"></div></a><div style=3D"clear:both"></div>
Models can move through different categories of <b>terrain feature</b> as f=
ollows:<br><ul><li><b>Exposed/Light:</b> All models can move horizontally a=
nd vertically through <b><a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rule=
s/core-rules/#Exposed">exposed</a></b> and <b><a href=3D"https://wahapedia.=
ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Light">light terrain features</a></b>.</=
li><li><b>Dense:</b><br><ul><li><span class=3D"kwb">INFANTRY</span>/<span c=
lass=3D"kwb">BEASTS</span>/<span class=3D"kwb">SWARM</span>/<span class=3D"=
kwb">MOBILE</span> models can move horizontally through <b><b><a href=3D"ht=
tps://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Dense">dense terrain fea=
tures</a></b></b>.</li><li><span class=3D"kwb">INFANTRY</span>/<span class=
=3D"kwb">BEASTS</span>/<span class=3D"kwb">SWARM</span> models can move ver=
tically through <b>dense terrain features</b>.</li><li>Other models can mov=
e horizontally through <b>dense terrain features</b> provided that all sect=
ions of that <b>terrain feature</b> that the moving model=E2=80=99s base wo=
uld move through are 2" or less in height. Otherwise, the moving model must=
 move vertically to ascend or descend such sections. They cannot move throu=
gh ceilings and floors while doing so, and they cannot end that move on any=
 surface of that <b>terrain feature</b> that is not on ground level (see be=
low).</li></ul></li></ul><br><div class=3D"BreakInsideAvoid frameDark Corne=
rSeeAlso"><span class=3D"hi_custom">SEE ALSO</span><br><ul><li>Solid Terrai=
n and Movement  <span class=3D"kwn"><span class=3D"tooltip00060" data-toolt=
ip-content=3D"#tooltip_content00060"><span class=3D"tt kwbu">13.06.01</span=
></span></span></li></ul></div>
</span></div><div class=3D"tooltip_templates"><span id=3D"tooltip_content00=
062"><div class=3D"tooltip_header">Moving a Model in a Straight Line</div><=
a href=3D"https://wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Moving-a-Mod=
el-in-a-Straight-Line"><div class=3D"tooltip_link"></div></a><div style=3D"=
clear:both"></div>
Each time you move a model in a straight line, move it horizontally across =
the battlefield. Measure from the same point on its base at the start and e=
nd of that move, and add that distance to any other distance it has moved s=
ince its unit began that move. The distance moved cannot be greater than th=
e <b>maximum distance</b> of that <b>move type</b>.
</span></div><div class=3D"tooltip_templates"><span id=3D"tooltip_content00=
063"><div class=3D"tooltip_header">Rotating a Model</div><a href=3D"https:/=
/wahapedia.ru/wh40k11ed/the-rules/core-rules/#Rotating-a-Model"><div class=
=3D"tooltip_link"></div></a><div style=3D"clear:both"></div>
Each time you rotate a model, turn it any amount around the centre of its b=
ase, while keeping it upright. Note that rotating a model does not count to=
wards the distance it has moved.
